The published artifact, AppleIroh.xcframework, is a static library. It contains
compiled code from third-party crates whose licences travel with it.

iroh — https://github.com/n0-computer/iroh
    Licensed under either of Apache License 2.0 or MIT, at the user's option.
    iroh itself ships a LICENSE-BSD3 that is an attribution rather than its
    licence: parts of its socket code are derived from Tailscale
    (https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale), BSD-3-Clause.

tokio — https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio
    MIT.

The full dependency set, pinned, is Cargo.lock. `cargo tree` over that lock
enumerates every crate compiled into the artifact, and `cargo about` or an
equivalent will produce the complete licence manifest for a distribution that
needs one.
